		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=22192#p22192"><![CDATA[
I think the distinction should be between velocity versus acceleration constraints instead of impulses versus forces. In other words, does the engine try to solve acceleration constraints? Baraff showed that satisfaction of acceleration constraints can lead to infinite constraint forces. A typical physics engine does not attempt to satisfy acceleration constraints, leading to finite constraint forces. The downside is that we are restricted to a first order integrator.<br><br>That said, I don't know if Newton uses velocity or acceleration constraints.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=12">Erin Catto</a> — Mon Feb 21, 2011 12:50 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
